    correctAnswer: 3,
    explanation: 'R8 compatibility mode (default before AGP 8.0) mimics ProGuard behavior for maximum library compatibility. R8 full mode (default since AGP 8.0) enables additional optimizations: enum unboxing, more aggressive tree shaking, class merging, and may remove interface implementations. This can break reflection-dependent code lacking keep rules.',
    codeSnippet: '// build.gradle.kts (AGP 8.0+: full mode is default)\nandroid {\n    buildTypes {\n        release {\n            isMinifyEnabled = true\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// To opt into full mode on older AGP:\n// gradle.properties\nandroid.enableR8.fullMode=true\n\n// Full mode may break:\n// - ServiceLoader patterns\n// - Reflection on interface hierarchies\n// - Libraries using Class.forName()\n\n// Fix with keep rules:\n-keep interface com.example.Plugin\n-keep class * implements com.example.Plugin',
