    question: 'What are the implications of using collectAsStateWithLifecycle vs collectAsState for Flow collection in Compose?',
    options: ['They are identical', 'collectAsStateWithLifecycle only works with StateFlow', 'collectAsStateWithLifecycle stops collection when the lifecycle goes below the specified state (default STARTED), preventing unnecessary work and UI updates when the app is backgrounded. collectAsState collects unconditionally while in composition.', 'collectAsState is deprecated in favor of collectAsStateWithLifecycle'],
    correctAnswer: 2,
    explanation: 'collectAsState keeps collecting from the Flow even when the app is in the background (between onStop and onStart). collectAsStateWithLifecycle pauses collection when the lifecycle drops below STARTED, saving resources and preventing updates to an invisible UI. Google recommends collectAsStateWithLifecycle for all production code.',
    codeSnippet: '// Recommended: lifecycle-aware collection\n@Composable\nfun UserScreen(viewModel: UserViewModel) {\n    val uiState by viewModel.uiState\n        .collectAsStateWithLifecycle()\n    // Stops collecting when app backgrounded\n    // Resumes when app foregrounded\n}\n\n// Not recommended for production:\n@Composable\nfun UserScreen(viewModel: UserViewModel) {\n    val uiState by viewModel.uiState\n        .collectAsState(initial = UiState.Loading)\n    // Keeps collecting even when backgrounded\n    // Wastes resources, may cause errors\n}\n\n// Dependency:\n// implementation("androidx.lifecycle:lifecycle-runtime-compose:2.7.0")',
