    explanation: 'WorkManager provides LiveData and Flow APIs to observe work state (ENQUEUED, RUNNING, SUCCEEDED, FAILED, CANCELLED) and intermediate progress. Workers call setProgress(Data) to report progress. In Compose, use getWorkInfoByIdFlow() with collectAsStateWithLifecycle() for reactive progress tracking.',
    codeSnippet: '@Composable\nfun UploadProgress(workId: UUID) {\n    val workManager = WorkManager.getInstance(LocalContext.current)\n    val workInfo by workManager\n        .getWorkInfoByIdFlow(workId)\n        .collectAsStateWithLifecycle(initialValue = null)\n\n    when (workInfo?.state) {\n        WorkInfo.State.RUNNING -> {\n            val progress = workInfo?.progress\n                ?.getInt("percent", 0) ?: 0\n            LinearProgressIndicator(progress = progress / 100f)\n            Text("Uploading: $progress%")\n        }\n        WorkInfo.State.SUCCEEDED -> Text("Upload complete!")\n        WorkInfo.State.FAILED -> Text("Upload failed")\n        else -> Text("Waiting...")\n    }\n}\n\n// In Worker:\nclass UploadWorker(...) : CoroutineWorker(...) {\n    override suspend fun doWork(): Result {\n        for (i in 0..100 step 10) {\n            setProgress(workDataOf("percent" to i))\n            uploadChunk(i)\n        }\n        return Result.success()\n    }\n}',
