    question: 'How do alignment lines work in custom Compose layouts and how do you create custom ones?',
    options: ['Alignment lines only work with Text composables', 'Alignment lines are named positions within a layout that other layouts can align to. FirstBaseline and LastBaseline are built-in. You can create custom ones by providing them in the layout() block and reading them via Placeable[alignmentLine].', 'Custom alignment lines require Android 13+', 'Alignment lines are the same as gravity in the View system'],
